- Projects willing to comply with AGPL-3 obligations:
    (a) Any work you convey that is based on watching-zenoh must itself
        be licensed as a whole under AGPL-3 — the entire combined work,
        not merely the watching-zenoh portion. Dynamic linking does not
        avoid this; there is no LGPL-style "relink" carve-out.
    (b) AGPL-3 §13: if you MODIFY watching-zenoh and let users interact
        with your modified version REMOTELY over a network, you must
        offer those users the Corresponding Source of your version, at
        no charge, from a network server. Running it as a service is
        not a way around (a) — this is the clause that distinguishes
        AGPL from plain GPL.
    (c) For "User Products" (consumer devices, embedded firmware),
        AGPL-3 §6 ("anti-tivoization") requires providing the user with
        the Installation Information needed to install a modified
        watching-zenoh on that device — signing keys, build
        instructions, install procedure.
    (d) Modifications to watching-zenoh's own source must be
        distributed under AGPL-3 (no private modifications under this
        option once you convey or serve the result).

If any of (a) through (d) is unacceptable for your product, use
Option 2 (Commercial License) instead.

