================================================================================
ZENOH WIRE PROTOCOL: Interop only (no shared code)
================================================================================

watching-zenoh is an independent reimplementation of the Zenoh 1.x
wire protocol (peer + client modes, zenoh-pico parity scope per
ARCHITECTURE.md §2). No code is shared with the upstream Zenoh
(Apache-2.0 OR EPL-2.0) or zenoh-pico (Apache-2.0 OR EPL-2.0)
projects — interoperability is at the wire-format level only, which
is not a copyrightable artifact.

================================================================================
Quick Decision Guide
================================================================================

| Your Situation                                | License Choice | Cost            |
|-----------------------------------------------|----------------|-----------------|
| Open source project, AGPL-compatible          | AGPL-3.0+      | FREE            |
| Internal use, never conveyed and never served | AGPL-3.0+      | FREE            |
| Proprietary commercial product                | Commercial     | Contact         |
| Network service on a modified watching-zenoh  | Commercial     | Contact         |
| Embedded firmware (signed / locked devices)   | Commercial     | Contact         |
| Private modifications to watching-zenoh       | Commercial     | Contact         |
| Redistribute as SDK / rebranded product       | Commercial     | Contact         |

"Internal use" is narrow on purpose: AGPL-3 obligations attach when you
CONVEY a covered work, and — under §13 — when you let users interact
with a MODIFIED version over a network. Running an unmodified
watching-zenoh for yourself triggers neither.

